{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1400, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nA positive integer X is called a good integer if and only if it satisfies the following condition:\n\n- There exists a pair of positive integers (a,b) such that X = 2^a \\times b^2.\n\nFor example, 400 is a good integer because 400 = 2^2 \\times 10^2.\nGiven a positive integer N, find the number of good integers between 1 and N, inclusive.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the number of good integers between 1 and N, inclusive.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1 \\leq N \\leq 10^{18}\n- N is an integer.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n20\n\nSample Output 1\n\n5\r\n\nThere are five good integers between 1 and 20: 2, 4, 8, 16, and 18.\r\nThus, print 5.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n400\n\nSample Output 2\n\n24\n\nSample Input 3\n\n1234567890\n\nSample Output 3\n\n42413\r\n\nNote that the input might not fit in a 32-bit integer type.\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1431, "char_start": 1412, "quote": "Input:\n20\nOutput:\n5", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1464, "char_start": 1443, "quote": "Input:\n400\nOutput:\n24", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 1507, "char_start": 1476, "quote": "Input:\n1234567890\nOutput:\n42413", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "42e107a5e94513c915a093514d8cc76e4ca2466d28cf2b622494f827c1d33423", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "e9755adcef5a24064ef8c23baf92d24a97eac8e33e35c8c491eb9a62c41cc1bf", "seq": 2}
